# Nothing secret belongs in this repository.
.env
.env.*
# The examples are the exception and must be committed. `.env.*` above swallowed them,
# which was found on 23 September when `git add` silently staged nothing: an .env.example
# that is ignored is an .env.example that does not exist for anybody cloning the
# repository, and it is the one file that says which variables the service needs.
# Nothing in either example is a real value.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/next-env.d.ts
web/package-lock.json
service/.env
service/__pycache__/
service/**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
